    pr_ref:  # 4716
    description: "THE CLASS ITEM. Six ADR-0017 artifacts were closed done on \"N tests, 100%\ncoverage\" while having no production caller:\n\n  - section 3a DDG propagation (results computed, discarded)\n  - section 4a infer_summary -- zero production callers\n  - section 4b load_function_summaries -- zero production callers\n  - section 7a is_field_tainted -- zero production callers\n  - the Rust and TypeScript def/use extractors -- zero production callers\n  - section 3c mixed-coverage verdict -- confidence is write-only\n\n_sink_module_compatible, retired 2026-08-01, was the first found member of this\nfamily, not an isolated case. Every reference in all seven was PROSE: an ADR\nsection, a sibling module docstring, a CLI docstring, test docstrings. None of\nit is checkable by any gate the project has. Each parsed, linted, and sat at\n100% coverage held there by its own tests.\n\nREMEDY: an executable gate. A production symbol whose only reachability is its\nown test module fails CI. This is the code-reachability twin of the\nclosure-evidence guard, and the recurrence-prevention for the whole family.\nWithout it, the individual items above are the next site rather than the class\n(R8: file the CLASS, not the next site)."  # 4716
    fields: {}  # 4716
- op: discuss  # 61b4
  at: '2026-08-05T06:22:36Z'  # 61b4
  by: agent  # 61b4
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 61b4
  clock: 2  # 61b4
  nonce: 61b4  # 61b4
  message: "ONE FAMILY MEMBER RETIRED BY WIRING IT, not by deleting it (PR #213). _extract_callee_language had zero production callers and a docstring asserting it is \"used by sink/source matching to filter cross-language pollution\" - a textbook member of this class. It is now a real consumer: _match_propagation_entry takes the language whose catalogue built the index and refuses a foreign callee, which is exactly what the docstring described. A test asserts the matcher references it, so the prose claim now has the executable trigger R16 requires. NOTE FOR THIS GATE DESIGN: this member was found by inspection, not by any gate, and it had been sitting at 100% coverage with its own passing unit test - which is precisely the reachability pattern this item exists to catch. Its measured effect is ZERO flows on the 9-repo cohort (208 cross-language taint call edges, none matching a wrong-language sink), so a gate keyed on behaviour change would not have flagged it either; only reachability would."  # 61b4
- op: discuss  # ce25
  at: '2026-08-05T10:19:59Z'  # ce25
  by: agent  # ce25
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ce25
  clock: 3  # ce25
  nonce: ce25  # ce25
  message: "RE-SCOPED ON MEASUREMENT 2026-08-05. OWNER RULING: STOP HERE, DOCUMENT, DO NOT BUILD THE\nGATE AS FILED. The remedy in this item is not implementable as written, and the measurement\nthat says so is below. The item stays OPEN because the need is real; what changes is the\ndesign and its prerequisite.\n\n*** THE POSITIVE CONTROL IS 3 OF 10, AND THAT ALONE FORBIDS BUILDING ON THIS SUBSTRATE. ***\nThe obvious implementation is dead-code-maybe, which already computes exactly this cohort.\nRun against the ten ADR-0017 family members this item names as its motivation:\n    TaintCatalog.match_source / match_sink / match_sanitizer -> flagged test_only   (3)\n    load_function_summaries -> correctly ABSENT; it has 2 production call sites now,\n        genuinely fixed by PR #197 during this campaign                              (1)\n    infer_summary / is_field_tainted / select_ddg_targets -> ABSENT, and each still\n        has ZERO production call sites (verified by grep over packages/*/src)        (3)\n    the rust and typescript def/use extractors, and the section 3a discard -> not\n        function-shaped members, out of scope for any symbol-reachability gate       (3)\nSo of the members a symbol gate COULD catch, it catches 3 of 6 and misses 3 that are\nlive-inert today. A gate that misses half of its own motivating examples is not a gate.\n\n*** THE CAUSE IS STRUCTURAL AND IT IS NOT A BUG. *** All three misses carry\nis_exported=True, and the production seed set is entrypoints PLUS exported public API.\nThat is deliberate and correct in general -- an exported symbol may have callers outside\nthe analysis scope, which is WI-zafab filter 3's stated rationale -- but it means A PUBLIC\nFUNCTION WITH ZERO IN-REPO CALLERS CAN NEVER BE FLAGGED. The ADR-0017 family is exactly\nthat shape: exported module-level functions nobody calls. Verified on the map:\n    infer_summary        is_exported=True   function   function_summaries/__init__.py\n    is_field_tainted     is_exported=True   function   taint.py\n    select_ddg_targets   is_exported=True   function   cfg.py\n    select_by_tokens     is_exported=False  function   compact.py   <- so it IS flagged\n    estimate_node_tokens is_exported=False  function   compact.py   <- so it IS flagged\n\n*** AND THE COHORT IS DOMINATED BY DISPATCH, NOT BY DEADNESS. *** 1747 test-only\ncandidates on the self-tree (1859 over all production symbols; the 112 gap is the FP\ndemoters). Shape split:\n    598  Class.method            -- analyzer protocol methods\n   1147  private module function -- _helpers of those methods\n      2  public bare function    -- the only shape the ADR-0017 family has\nBy package: lang-mainstream 585, lang-extended1 400, lang-common 384, tracker 233,\ncore 144. Sampled 25 at random and they are NixAnalyzer.extract_edges_from_file,\nPerlAnalyzer.extract_symbols_from_file, VhdlAnalyzer.extract_symbols_from_file and their\nprivate helpers -- LIVE production code reached through the analyzer registry, which the\nstatic call graph does not model. A shrink-only ratchet over that population would fire on\nevery new analyzer helper, which is the single most common change in this repository, and\nwould be rubber-stamped into the baseline. A rubber-stamped ratchet is worse than none: it\nteaches the reflex that this gate is noise.\n\n*** SO THE GATE AS WORDED WOULD FAIL CI ~1747 TIMES ON DAY ONE WHILE MISSING THE ONES IT\nWAS WRITTEN FOR. *** Both halves are disqualifying and they are independent.\n\n*** RE-SCOPED DESIGN, for whoever picks this up. ***\n1. The reachability question is NOT \"is this reachable from the production seeds\". It is\n   the one this item's own title states: DOES EVERY DIRECT CALLER OF THIS SYMBOL LIVE IN A\n   TEST MODULE. That question is immune to the is_exported seeding, because it asks about\n   callers rather than about seeds, and it is the question that catches a public function\n   with tests and no production caller.\n2. It needs a demotion arm for PROTOCOL / REGISTRY DISPATCH, or the 598 + 1147 analyzer\n   symbols drown it. The repo already has the two shapes this would extend: view_func\n   seeding (WI-vuton) and the inheritance-based virtual-dispatch demotion. The missing one\n   is the analyzer registry itself.\n3. PREREQUISITE, and it is the honest price: hypergumbo does not model its own plugin\n   registry as reachability. Until it does, ANY test-only-reachability signal on this\n   repository is dominated by dispatch. That is a real feature -- it would benefit every\n   repo with a plugin registry -- and it deserves its own run rather than being tacked\n   onto the end of a taint campaign. R17 applies: price the recursion before entering it.\n\n*** THE PREREQUISITE THAT DID SHIP: WI-jozah. *** A gate needs per-item attribution to key\non, and dead-code-maybe emitted the cohort as a summary COUNT only. Each candidate now\ncarries a reachability field, and a second denominator ships with it because the two\npopulations differ (1859 over all production symbols vs 1747 over emitted candidates).\nEvery number in this note was measured through that field. Without it, none of the above\nwas answerable.\n\n*** WHAT IS STILL TRUE AND WHY THE ITEM STAYS OPEN. *** The family this item was filed on\nis real, it grew under inspection three separate times, and every member was closed done on\n100% coverage with prose as its only evidence. R16 is satisfied only by written triggers\ntoday. Nothing here weakens the case for the gate; it establishes that the gate needs a\ndifferent reachability question and one modelling prerequisite, and that building it on the\nexisting dead-code machinery would have produced a green gate over a structurally impossible\nsignal -- the shape this project has already been bitten by more than once."  # ce25
